    oe:aboutDisease oed:cirrhosis ;
    oe:answerText "Cholestatic pruritus is common and undertreated in primary biliary cholangitis (PBC) and negatively affects patients' lives. We aimed to evaluate the safety and efficacy of linerixibat, an ileal bile acid transporter inhibitor, as a specific antipruritic therapy in patients with PBC."^^xsd:string ;
